/// Consent-surface risk classification for a Permission (#60). Drives how
/// prominently a permission request is rendered on plugin install/update
/// consent surfaces and whether the Critical+required second-factor gate
/// fires (#59 install-validation steps 13–14).
///
/// Canonical rubric (#60):
/// - Critical: mutating auth/roles/permissions, user PII at scale, audit
///   log mutation, security-control mutation
/// - High: cross-household reads, user listing, household membership
///   management, audit log read access, mass notification send
/// - Medium: cross-user-within-household reads, financial/transaction data
/// - Low: scoped reads within the actor's own context, household-scoped
///   writes to user-owned resources
///
/// Classification is seed-declared (prisma/seeds/roles-permissions.seed.ts,
/// authoritative on re-run); admin reclassification is out of scope (#60).
enum RiskLevel {
  Low
  Medium
  High
  Critical
}
